#   stays because build\common.ps1 reads the .slnx with `dotnet sln list`, which SDK 8 cannot.
#   The gallery folder then resolves SDK 9.0.321, not the 8.0.3xx the spec expected.
# - Request: the seed script opens /account/apikeys?forceApiKeys=true. Without it the page redirects
#   every user to Trusted Publishing; the Trusted Publishing page's own "API keys" link adds it.
# - Request: the API key is created with an 8-day expiry (one of the form's choices). The shipped
#   flags.json enables NuGetGallery.ApiKeyReduction, which treats keys lasting over 30 days as expiring
#   on 2026-11-01, so a 365-day key would be expired on creation.
